module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value that carries optionality -- a CardOptional T? or the nominal Optional coproduct -- stands at a position whose declared type is Required and non-generic: a direct-call argument, a list element, or a member of a list literal whose type was elected from a Required head element. Absent inhabits no Required type, so the program has no meaning at that position; the floor obligation 'values inhabit declared types' (DESIGN 4b, the floor first) is broken.",
    "RECEIPT, gunbc#11626 (2026-09-19): NUMERIC-BIT-0 #11643 changed std.encoding base64_encode to return String?; the approval_device_wire site from #11660 calls join([prefix, base64_encode(..)], \"\"). No diagnostic. The regenerated vectors.json on CRYPTO-0's #11647 branch rendered the URL path as `id-Present { value: ZXNj... }` instead of `id-ZXNj...`, and the ci-auto-heal bot committed those bytes (e7b8ad2 on session/royal-stag-544) -- fabricated plausible output reaching a committed fixture.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, measured on main 3fabccc35f: a String? at a String direct-call parameter and at a List<String> argument's element compiled with only an advisory, v1.compiler.infer declared_type_inhabitance filing both under UndecidableOptionalCarrier -- a reason written for the LIFT direction (a T standing in an Optional<T> position) and applied to the converse, which is decided. A list literal with NO expected type (join's receiver) typed as List<head> and judged no member at all: 0 diagnostics. Neighbouring walls were silent by construction: kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch bails unless the ACTUAL is a kernel type, and nominal_call_arg_brand_mismatch requires equal structural-carrier templates.",
    "SECOND HALF OF THE SAME CLASS: the interpreter's rendering of a variant value into a String context (join, concat, interpolation) produces the Debug-shaped text `Present { value: ... }` rather than refusing. That is the runtime realization of the same invalid state; the compile wall makes it unreachable for Accepted programs at the judged positions, and the interpreter arm itself remains a mitigation-rung obligation: a String context receiving a non-String value should refuse typed, never stringify.",
    "POPULATION (deletion is the census): 94 sites refused and fixed in the change filing this row -- 11 in the required-regen self-compile closure, 72 more in the generated_artifact_gate closure found by CI heal-generated-artifacts, and 11 more found by the required floor (devboot produce, floor_cost_distribution, spark serving_incarnation_observe, std.selected_witness_bundle, and two witness files). Nearly all are `.first()` (bare value or Null at runtime) consumed as the element type behind a count guard; the remainder are a Percent? policy field read as Percent (gunbc.oomd_install, now a single-authority datum) and list indexing. Two refusals were NOT defects: `match opt { null => a  v => b }` bound v at the scrutinee's own T?, so the wall carried a match-narrowing rule (a Bind arm after an unguarded Absent arm binds the present type) rather than editing correct code. The census is closure-scoped: a remote whole-root compile refuses on WholeCorpusCompileBudgetUnreadable by design, so the population is what the required gates compile.",
    "SECOND RECEIPT, review 73175 on gunbc#12677 (2026-09-30): `AccountTripNativeCauseNumericCode { code: parse_int(..) }` for a field declared `code: Int` compiled with no row and the floor stayed green. The site was repaired in that change; the class was the record-literal field residual this row already named, and the same hole stood at the declared return, the let annotation and the data initializer.",
    "THE CHAIN (DESIGN 6b), and why the repair is producers rather than a guard. The relation that decides an optional at a required position already existed and was already single: v1.compiler.infer optional_produced_at_required_declared, consulted first by declared_type_inhabitance. What was missing was upstream of it: the record-literal field chain and declared_type_conformance_diags (declared return, early return, let annotation, data initializer) never built an obligation, and compared the two types through node_type_compatible, which reads the type name and not return_cardinality. That relation is undirected -- it is also asked of branch pairs and of the lift direction -- so teaching it cardinality would have refused correct code; optional-into-required is a DIRECTED fact about a declared position, which is what DeclaredTypeObligation carries. The earliest unjustified boundary is therefore the absent producer, and the repair is optional_at_required_obligation_diags: those four seams build the same obligation, consult the same predicate, and emit the same DeclaredTypeNotInhabited naming the position, the field or binding, and both cardinalities. The undeclared list-literal member producer was folded onto it, so no second rendering of the verdict remains.",
    "TWO FABRICATED REFUSALS FOUND BY THE CENSUS AND REPAIRED AT THE PREDICATE, NOT AT SITES. (a) A coproduct that declares its own `Absent` arm (std.upsert_decision ObservationVerdict, gunbc.host.host_converge ConvergeVerdict): the bare arm is typed as the kernel Optional coproduct, so the produced side is optional BY NAME ONLY. Sixteen correct sites newly refused, and six more already stood refused on main at the direct-call argument in test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_cli_witness_test, a fabricated refusal the first landing of this wall shipped. The predicate now abstains when the produced side carries no CardOptional and the declared coproduct owns `Absent` or `Present`. The defect it stands in for is upstream and open: variant-reference election ignores the declared coproduct and chooses the kernel Optional's Absent. Its owner is the value-position identity lane (deep-bee-18, session eager-ibex-722, routed by quiet-gull-780 on gunbc#12791); this row does not repair it. (b) An index access: v1.compiler.infer_access types `xs[i]` optional while its Rust realization is the bare element, and the seed's own tokenizer (v1.tokenize source_code_point, code_point_at) returns `chars[pos]` at a declared Int, as the note on code_point_at predicted. The second-generation regeneration refused on exactly those two. The optionality of an index value is not established across the two acceptance paths, so a value whose tail expression is an index access raises no obligation at the four new positions (expr_value_is_index_access).",
    "POPULATION OF THE SECOND LANDING (the whole-root compile differential; the instrument is named on gunbc.rung_drop.compiler_change_refusals_land_outside_every_compiled_closure, `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --target dag --repository gunbc --measured-root-demands tools/whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands.json`, base and head run sequentially on one frozen tree and joined on verbatim message plus location). Every newly refused identity is listed on the change that filed this receipt, each repaired or dispositioned there; the counts are that join's and are not restated here. The shapes: `.first()` / `.last()` / `first(..)` consumed as the element behind a length guard (the large majority, as in the first landing); `parse_int` into an Int field twice more, the exact specimen; a `T?` policy field read as `T`; and one explicit `Present { .. }` wrapper returned where the coproduct itself was declared. SCOPE, stated because it is narrower than WHOLE CORPUS: the join covers the dag-primary population only. A src/v2-primary whole-root compile refuses at admission with WholeCorpusCompileUnmeasuredRoot, so src/v2 modules are covered only where the dag root reaches them, and the modules that compile enters in the name census only are not covered at all. Both are UNMEASURED populations, not zeros: nothing here says they hold no optional at a required position.",
    "THE INDEX CARVE-OUT IS A DECLARED RESIDUAL POPULATION, COUNTED AT IDENTITY GRAIN, NOT A SILENT EXCLUSION. Membership: a value whose tail expression is an index access standing at a record-literal field, declared return, let annotation or data initializer whose declared type is Required. MEASURED MEMBERS, six, each refused by the wall before the exclusion and admitted after it: v1.tokenize source_code_point (declared return) and v1.tokenize code_point_at (declared return), found by the second-generation regeneration; gunbc.floor_cost_distribution parse_claim_cost_line, four record-literal fields (identity and module, in each of its two row literals), found by the dag-primary whole-root compile. The instrument for the dag-primary members is the head-before-exclusion side of the differential named above; nothing outside that population or the seed's own sources was measured, so six is the measured membership and not a bound on the class. WHAT IS LOST: at those sites an out-of-range index reaches a Required position as an absent value on the interpretation path with no refusal, which is this row's invalid state. WHY IT IS NOT REPAIRED AT THE SITES: eliminating the optional with a match authors an elimination the Rust realization of an index (the bare element) cannot satisfy; the disagreement is its own class, gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.list_index_typed_optional_but_realized_as_the_bare_element. TRIGGER, THE CAPABILITY: the typing and the realization of `xs[i]` agree -- the index is typed optional AND realized optional on every target, or an index is admitted only where it is proven in bounds and is then typed as the element. Either is sufficient to delete v1.compiler.infer expr_value_is_index_access, at which point the six members refuse or are proven and leave. ENROLLED: test.claim.optional_at_required_position_witness_test an_index_access_at_a_required_position_is_the_declared_residual pins the admission and flips to a refusal count when the trigger lands.",
    "RESIDUALS, named. (1) The index population above. (2) Arguments of BUILTIN and method calls: the direct-call seam judges declared functions, so `parse_int(s: lines.first())` and join's receiver are unjudged. (3) A list literal whose HEAD element is optional elects List<T?>. (4) The five DeclaredTypePosition members with no producer (map value, variant payload, cast target, parameter default, callable return). (5) The interpreter's String-context rendering of a variant, unchanged from the first landing. (6) The v2 judge: v2.std.inhabitance answers UndecidableOptionalCarrier for a cardinality node on EITHER side and v2.compiler.infer admits that verdict, so v2 admits an optional at a required position; read from source, not executed, and reported to the owning lane rather than repaired here.",
    "THE V2 ROUTE, a separate path with its own rung (2026-09-30). v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance carried the same misfiling: inhabitance_node_undecidable_reason answered UndecidableOptionalCarrier for a Cardinality type node on EITHER side, so a produced T? at a declared required type was admitted with an advisory. It was not reachable from source until gunbc#12777, because infer refused any tree carrying a Cardinality node for descent first (measured on main and on gunbc#12566: infer_descent_not_derived for `fn f(x: Int?) -> Int { x }`); with that change the program was ACCEPTED. The relation now refuses the pair by its own reason, inhabitance_optional_produced_at_required_declared. CURRENT RUNG on the v2 resolve-to-infer route: structurally guaranteed where the declared type is a kernel value type (an atom the judge denotes), at a declared return and at a record field, both executed from source text by v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_optional_at_required_witness_test. COUNTED, NOT REFUSED: a produced optional at a declared declaration reference, a declared Instantiation or a declared type variable, because the relation unfolds no alias and cannot know those are required (`type Maybe = Int?` is a declaration reference); trigger: the relation reads a declared type's resolved declaration, the capability gunbc#12726 PR2 provides. NOT YET ON THE ROUTE: a direct-call argument, because a named call's callee is not typed by its declaration (gunbc#12506); the relation refuses the pair, and the route claim is owed when that lands.",
    "HARM: silent wrongness, outside the ladder -- the output is plausible bytes, not a crash, and it was committed as a fixture by an automated heal.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent, below the floor. CURRENT RUNG, at the grain of source to v1 acceptance: structurally guaranteed for a non-index optional value at the direct-call argument, declared list element, undeclared list-literal member, record-literal field, declared return (trailing expression and early return), let annotation and data initializer -- DeclaredTypeNotInhabited naming position, subject, declared and produced types with cardinality. Silent at the residual positions above, so the class as a whole is not at that rung and this row does not claim it. CEILING: structurally guaranteed (typecheck refusal); decidable from the two resolved types.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, as capabilities. FIRST: the index model and its realization agree (an index realizes as an optional, or types as its element), sufficient to delete expr_value_is_index_access and flip its enrolled claim. SECOND: variant-reference election consults the declared coproduct, sufficient to delete the by-name-only exclusion. THIRD: builtin and method call arguments raise a DeclaredTypeObligation. FOURTH: the four cardinality-only positions hand their obligation to declared_type_obligation_diags, deleting their older chains. Fixtures: test.claim.optional_at_required_position_witness_test.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-09-29, AN UNJUDGED POSITION NOT IN THE LIST ABOVE: FIELD PROJECTION. A field read through an Optional is admitted: `xs.first().id`, where `.first()` produces T? and Absent has no `id` field. The same `.first()` at a direct-call argument refuses. Found by review 72657 on gunbc#12572, at test.claim.machine_shape_catalog_integration_witness `memory.first().id` (and `.transfer_grain`). The whole-corpus compile that refused that file's call-argument sites reported nothing at those reads. That is a silent below-floor admission: whatever the interpreter does at the projection, no Accepted program should hold it, and the compiler does not decide it. The discriminating pair is in test.claim.optional_field_read_admission_gap_witness_test: one source shape is compiled twice, once consuming `.first()` at a field read (admitted today, zero blocking rows) and once at a call argument (refused, DeclaredTypeNotInhabited). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, added to the one above: the field-projection position routes through the same relation. The admission claim then flips to a regression control asserting the refusal.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
